    <a href="#downloads-overview">Statistics</a>
    <a href="#downloads-related">Connected Resources</a>
  </nav>

  <!-- SECTION 1: GLOBUS PUBLIC COLLECTION \(SCINet - JUNO\) -->
  <section id="downloads-globus" class="mgdb-panel globus-hero-panel" aria-labelledby="globus-panel-heading">
    <div class="globus-badge-row">
      <span class="globus-tag-badge">High-Throughput Data Transfer</span>
      <span class="globus-subtag-badge">USDA SCINet HPC Infrastructure</span>
    </div>
    <h2 id="globus-panel-heading" class="mgdb-panel-title">MaizeGDB Public Collection \(SCINet - JUNO\)</h2>
    <p class="mgdb-panel-lead">High-speed, multi-gigabit automated data transfer powered by Globus. Ideal for multi-gigabyte to multi-terabyte datasets including complete genome assemblies, pre-indexed browser tracks, intermediate pipeline outputs, massive variant matrices, and AI/ML models.</p>

    <!-- GLOBUS COLLECTION IDENTITY CARD -->
    <div class="globus-id-card">
      <div class="globus-id-icon-wrap">
        <svg width="48" height="48" viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
          <!-- Globus multi-node network graphic -->
          <polygon points="24,6 40,15 40,33 24,42 8,33 8,15" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="2.5" fill="#f0fdf4" />
          <circle cx="24" cy="6" r="3.5" fill="#15803d" />
          <circle cx="40" cy="15" r="3.5" fill="#15803d" />
          <circle cx="40" cy="33" r="3.5" fill="#15803d" />
          <circle cx="24" cy="42" r="3.5" fill="#15803d" />
          <circle cx="8" cy="33" r="3.5" fill="#15803d" />
          <circle cx="8" cy="15" r="3.5" fill="#15803d" />
          <circle cx="24" cy="24" r="5" fill="#ca8a04" />
          <line x1="24" y1="24" x2="24" y2="6" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="2" />
          <line x1="24" y1="24" x2="40" y2="15" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="2" />
          <line x1="24" y1="24" x2="40" y2="33" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="2" />
          <line x1="24" y1="24" x2="24" y2="42" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="2" />
          <line x1="24" y1="24" x2="8" y2="33" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="2" />
          <line x1="24" y1="24" x2="8" y2="15" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="2" />
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="globus-id-body">
        <div class="globus-header-flex">
          <h3 class="globus-collection-name">MaizeGDB Public Collection \(SCINet - JUNO\)</h3>
          <span class="globus-guest-chip">Guest Collection \(GCS\) on <strong>SCINet-Juno</strong></span>
        </div>

        <div class="globus-meta-grid">
          <div class="globus-meta-item">
            <span class="meta-label">Collection Owner&#58;</span>
            <span class="meta-value"><code>carson.andorf@scinet.usda.gov</code></span>
          </div>
          <div class="globus-meta-item">
            <span class="meta-label">Globus Domain Endpoint&#58;</span>
            <span class="meta-value">
              <code id="globus-domain-str">g-3126c1.67741c.a567.data.globus.org</code>
              <button type="button" class="copy-btn-inline" onclick="copyText\('globus-domain-str', this\)" title="Copy Domain">Copy</button>
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="globus-collection-desc">
          <strong>Dataset Scope&#58;</strong> This public collection provides unrestricted, read-only access to curated datasets from MaizeGDB. It hosts a comprehensive suite of genetics, genomics, and breeding data including whole-genome FASTA/GFF files, pre-formatted JBrowse tracks \(BigWig, BAM, CRAM, VCF\), intermediate pipeline analyses, high-density SNP matrices, and AI machine learning weights and inference outputs.
        </p>

        <div class="globus-actions-row">
          <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="https://app.globus.org/file-manager?origin_id=g-3126c1.67741c.a567.data.globus.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open in Globus Web App &#8599;</a>
          <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="https://g-3126c1.67741c.a567.data.globus.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Direct HTTPS Browse &#8599;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- GLOBUS HOW-TO CONNECTION GUIDE -->
    <div class="globus-guide-container">
      <h3 class="guide-heading">How to Connect &amp; Transfer Data via Globus</h3>

      <!-- Step Cards Grid -->
      <div class="globus-methods-grid">
        <!-- METHOD 1: WEB APP -->
        <article class="method-card">
          <div class="method-badge">Method 1 &bull; Web Interface</div>
          <h4>Globus Web App \(Interactive GUI\)</h4>
          <p>Ideal for point-and-click transfers between MaizeGDB and your personal workstation, university cluster, or cloud storage \(AWS S3, Google Drive, Box\).</p>
          <ol class="method-steps-list">
            <li>Navigate to <a href="https://app.globus.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">app.globus.org &#8599;</a> and log in with your institutional credentials or Globus ID.</li>
            <li>In the <strong>File Manager</strong> search bar, enter <code>MaizeGDB Public Collection \(SCINet - JUNO\)</code> or domain <code>g-3126c1.67741c.a567.data.globus.org</code>.</li>
            <li>Select the files or directories you wish to retrieve on the left pane.</li>
            <li>Select your target destination endpoint on the right pane and click <strong>Start Transfer</strong>. Globus manages checksum verification, fire-and-forget background transfer, and email notification upon completion.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>

        <!-- METHOD 2: CLI -->
        <article class="method-card">
          <div class="method-badge method-badge-blue">Method 2 &bull; Command Line</div>
          <h4>Globus CLI \(Automated Pipelines\)</h4>
          <p>Ideal for batch compute jobs, bioinformatic workflows, and scheduled cron synchronization scripts on high-performance computing clusters.</p>
          
          <div class="code-block-wrap">
            <div class="code-block-header">
              <span>Terminal Command Snippets</span>
              <button type="button" class="copy-btn-inline" onclick="copySnippet\('cli-snippet-1', this\)">Copy Code</button>
            </div>
            <pre><code id="cli-snippet-1"># 1. Install Globus CLI via pip or conda
pip install globus-cli

# 2. Authenticate session
globus login

# 3. List top-level directories in the MaizeGDB collection
globus ls g-3126c1.67741c.a567.data.globus.org:/

# 4. Initiate recursive background transfer to your local HPC endpoint
globus transfer g-3126c1.67741c.a567.data.globus.org:/genomes/ &lt;YOUR_ENDPOINT_ID&gt;:/scratch/maize/ --recursive --label "MaizeGDB Genome Sync"</code></pre>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 2: DIRECT HTTP BULK DOWNLOAD SERVER -->
  <section id="downloads-server" class="mgdb-panel" aria-labelledby="downloads-server-heading">
    <h2 id="downloads-server-heading" class="mgdb-panel-title">Direct HTTP Download Server &amp; Box Repository</h2>
    <p class="mgdb-panel-lead">Standard web-based FTP-style directories and institutional data stores for direct file downloads and automated scripting via curl or wget.</p>

    <div class="servers-grid">
      <!-- Card 1: HTTP Download Server -->
      <article class="server-card">
        <div class="server-card-top">
          <div class="server-icon-wrap">
            <img src="/images/maize_download.png" alt="MaizeGDB Download Server" />
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>MaizeGDB HTTP Download Server</h3>
            <span class="server-url-badge">https&#58;//download.maizegdb.org/</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="server-card-desc">Comprehensive open-access file tree holding all released B73 assemblies \(v1&ndash;v5\), 26 NAM founder inbreds, wild relatives, genetic maps, transcriptomics matrices, and supplementary publication files.</p>
        <div class="server-card-actions">
          <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="https://download.maizegdb.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Browse Download Server &#8599;</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Card 2: Box Data Store -->
      <article class="server-card">
        <div class="server-card-top">
          <div class="server-icon-wrap">
            <img src="/images/box_download.png" alt="MaizeGDB Box Data Store" />
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Institutional Box Data Store</h3>
            <span class="server-url-badge">iastate.app.box.com/v/maizegdb-public</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="server-card-desc">Public cloud storage repository dedicated to large machine learning models, neural network weights, deep learning datasets, and bundled NAM project JBrowse track archives.</p>
        <div class="server-card-actions">
          <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="https://iastate.app.box.com/v/maizegdb-public" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Browse Box Repository &#8599;</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

